  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Path difference introduced due to displacement of tube is given by<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>2x=10&nbsp;cm</mtext></math><br />Now&nbsp;due to one wavelength change, maxima/minima will be attained once hence for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;maxima's</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0629863.jpg\" style=\"width: 124px; height: 161px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>ΔP=10λ=10&nbsp;cm&nbsp;</mtext></math><br />So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&nbsp;λ=1&nbsp;cm&nbsp;</mtext></math></p>",
    "image": null
